# Scout architecture

## Layout

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `apps/server` | Ingest API, health-check runner, Postgres |
| `apps/dashboard` | Flutter Web UI |
| `packages/scout_models` | Shared types (events, health reports) |
| `scripts/` | Deploy, local `./dev`, Dart SDK fetch |
| `docs/agents/` | How we work, tracker, glossary |

SDK lives in **scout_logger_plus** (separate repo) — do not treat `packages/scout_logger_plus/` as this tree’s source of truth.

## Safe defaults

- Prefer extending existing types/routes/screens over new layers.
- Shared JSON shapes → `scout_models`, then server + dashboard.
- Deploy: `./deploy` (bundles Linux Dart SDK for health scripts).
- Local stack: `./dev` / `scripts/dev-local.sh`.

## Health checks (reminder)

Scripts run **on the Scout server**, not the user’s phone. Timeouts often mean network/geo, not a broken API. See `docs/MOBILE-SERVER-HEALTH.md`.
